From bee44385a528bba66abe1af553113ed9a703bf0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Hughes <tomhughes@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:24:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rand: Fix double-free on thread-local failure.

Backport of upstream bee44385a, first released in 0.20261020.0. It is
applied to every build, `fips` included, since FIPS builds compile the same
module source.

CRYPTO_set_thread_local invokes the destructor callback on the value
before returning zero on failure. In BCM_rand_bytes_with_additional_data
(updated in commit 364eef1863bf11e80a3fd8a603ba69f14b910fdb), calling
Delete(state) in the failure branch frees state a second time after
rand_thread_state_free has already freed it.

Remove the redundant Delete(state) call.
---
 crypto/fipsmodule/rand/rand.cc.inc | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crypto/fipsmodule/rand/rand.cc.inc b/crypto/fipsmodule/rand/rand.cc.inc
index 5d4fc9f39..839a03fcb 100644
--- a/crypto/fipsmodule/rand/rand.cc.inc
+++ b/crypto/fipsmodule/rand/rand.cc.inc
@@ -381,8 +381,8 @@ bcm_infallible bssl::BCM_rand_bytes_with_additional_data(
         !CRYPTO_set_thread_local(OPENSSL_THREAD_LOCAL_RAND, state,
                                  rand_thread_state_free)) {
       // If the system is out of memory, use an ephemeral state on the
-      // stack.
-      Delete(state);
+      // stack. `rand_thread_state_free` has already been called by
+      // `CRYPTO_set_thread_local` on failure.
       state = &stack_state;
     }
 
